{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I will distinguish.</b> Some say it is missing alef. The correct view is that it belongs to the class of he [as root letter] and its meaning is 'and I will separate.' By reason, Pharaoh now began to lighten Israel's labor, for when he saw that HaShem had made a distinction between Israel and Egypt, he feared to do them harm, since he needs them to go sacrifice lest a plague strike him. Do you not see that he now gives them permission to sacrifice in the land?" "And the meaning of 'for I am YHWH in the midst of the land': by way of parable, like the custom of kings to stand in the middle of their kingdom, to be close to the edges, just as HaShem created the heart of man, which is king over the entire body, in the middle, and the spirit of man in the middle of the body, as written: 'and forms the spirit of man within him' (Zechariah 12:1). And there are many proofs from nature for this; therefore it is written: 'Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, Elohim shines forth' (Psalms 50:2), for it is in the middle of the inhabited world, and the kingdom of HaShem is seen throughout the inhabited world."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:32:43.531782251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}